    "url": "https://mljar.com/",
    "text": "<div><div><div><p>Ask questions in plain English. Get real Python code, charts, and reproducible notebooks. Your data stays on your computer.</p><ul><li><span></span><span>Talk to your data using natural language</span></li><li><span></span><span>Let AI run machine learning experiments for you</span></li><li><span></span><span>Keep everything <strong>100% local and secure.</strong></span></li></ul><div><p>Download Studio</p><p>Read documentation</p></div></div><div><div><p>Users &amp; Companies</p><h2>Teams in academia and industry build with MLJAR</h2><p>From research labs to fast-moving product teams, people rely on MLJAR to analyze data and ship insights.</p></div><div><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p><p><img></p></div></div><div><p>Work With Your Own AI Data Analyst</p><h2>Ask questions. Get answers. Instantly.</h2><p>MLJAR Studio includes an AI assistant that understands your data and helps you explore it.<br>Ask questions in plain language and the AI will generate Python code, run it locally, and show the results.<br>You stay fully in control — every line of code is visible and reproducible.</p><ul><li><span></span><span>Ask questions about your data in natural language</span></li><li><span></span><span>Automatically generate and run Python analysis</span></li><li><span></span><span>Inspect and edit the code anytime</span></li><li><span></span><span>No external APIs required</span></li></ul></div><div><p>Let AI Run Machine Learning Experiments</p><h2>Automate your machine learning research</h2><p>Building good machine learning models requires many experiments. MLJAR Studio can run these experiments for you.<br>Its AI agent improves notebooks step-by-step, testing new ideas and searching for better models.</p><ul><li><span></span><span>Automatically tune machine learning models</span></li><li><span></span><span>Discover useful new features in your data</span></li><li><span></span><span>Compare models and track experiments</span></li><li><span></span><span>Generate explanations and reports</span></li></ul></div><div><p>AI Assistance Inside Your Notebook</p><h2>Code faster with AI by your side</h2><p>When working in notebooks, the AI assistant helps you write and improve code.<br>It suggests Python snippets, data transformations, and visualizations — but you always decide what runs.</p><ul><li><span></span><span>Smart Python suggestions</span></li><li><span></span><span>Faster data exploration</span></li><li><span></span><span>Full control over execution</span></li><li><span></span><span>Perfect for beginners and experts</span></li></ul></div><div><p>Turn Your Analysis into Interactive Apps</p><h2>Share your results as interactive web apps</h2><p>With one click you can turn your notebook into a web application.<br>Share dashboards, reports, and tools with your team - all hosted on your own infrastructure.<br>Powered by Mercury, our open-source framework.</p><ul><li><span></span><span>Convert notebooks to web apps</span></li><li><span></span><span>Self-host on your own server</span></li><li><span></span><span>Share results with colleagues</span></li><li><span></span><span>No cloud services required</span></li></ul><div><p>Check GitHub</p><p>Explore Apps</p></div></div><div><div><p>Why MLJAR Studio Is Different</p><h2>Built for privacy, control, and real data work</h2><p>Most AI tools require sending your data to the cloud. MLJAR Studio works differently. Everything runs on your machine, using real Python execution and fully reproducible notebooks.</p></div><div><div><h3>100% local execution</h3><p>Your data never leaves your computer.</p></div><div><h3>Real Python environment</h3><p>Not a toy interface - a full data science workspace.</p></div><div><h3>Fully reproducible workflows</h3><p>Every result can be reproduced from code.</p></div><div><h3>Self-hosted deployment</h3><p>Share results without relying on external services.</p></div></div></div><div><div><h2>Applied in Real-World Data Projects</h2><p>MLJAR tools have been used in a wide range of machine learning projects, including healthcare data analysis, financial modeling, manufacturing optimization, and many structured data problems.</p></div><ul><li>Healthcare</li><li>Manufacturing</li><li>Biotechnology</li><li>NLP</li><li>Pharma</li><li>Archaeology</li><li>AutoML</li><li>Computer Vision</li><li>Cybersecurity</li><li>Education</li><li>Green AI</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Physics</li><li>Responsible Ai</li></ul></div><div><div><h2>Built for people who work with data</h2><p>MLJAR Studio is perfect for:</p></div><div><div><h3>Data analysts exploring datasets</h3><p>Move faster with AI assistance, visual exploration, and notebook-friendly workflows.</p></div><div><h3>Data scientists running experiments</h3><p>Iterate with reproducible pipelines, model comparisons, and transparent Python execution.</p></div><div><h3>Researchers working with sensitive data</h3><p>Keep projects local while maintaining auditability and reproducibility.</p></div><div><h3>Teams that want AI without cloud risks</h3><p>Use AI capabilities in a controlled environment without exposing data to external services.</p></div></div></div><div><div><p></p><h2>Answers to Common Questions</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Does MLJAR Studio require cloud services?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Can I use local AI models?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Do I need programming experience?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Is MLJAR Studio just an AI tool?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>What type of data can I analyze?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Can I share my analysis with others?</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Is MLJAR Studio open source?</h2><p></p></div></div><div><h2>Start using AI for Data Analysis</h2><p>MLJAR Studio helps you analyze data with AI, run machine learning workflows, and build reproducible notebook-based results on your own computer.</p><p>Runs locally • Supports local LLMs</p><div><p>Download Studio</p><p>View Documentation</p></div></div></div></div>",
