    "url": "https://freegraphpaper.net/",
    "text": "<div><div><section><span><span></span> Free · No login · Instant PDF </span><p> Download free printable graph paper as a clean, print-ready PDF — from 5&nbsp;mm and 1/4&nbsp;inch grids to 1&nbsp;cm squares — or make your own custom graph paper in the browser. Beyond classic square grids you'll also find dot grid, isometric, hexagon, lined and Cornell notes paper, every sheet true to scale. </p><p>Create Custom PaperDraw on Graph Paper</p></section><section><div><div><h2>Popular graph paper templates</h2><p>The grids people print most — one click to a ready PDF.</p></div><p>All templates →</p></div><div><ul><!--[--><li>Graph PaperSquare grids in metric and imperial spacing for math, plotting and design.</li><li>Dot Grid PaperCalm dotted grids for bullet journals, sketching and lettering.</li><li>Isometric PaperTriangular 30° grids for 3D sketches, isometric drawing and CAD.</li><li>Hexagon PaperTessellated hex grids for games, organic chemistry and map design.</li><!--]--></ul></div></section><section><h2>Make and print your graph paper in 3 steps</h2><p> No sign-up, no watermark, no waiting on a server. Pick a graph paper template or build your own, preview it live, and download a print-ready PDF straight from your browser. </p><ol><!--[--><li><p>1</p><h3>Pick or customise</h3><p>Start from a ready-made graph paper template or set your own paper type, spacing, colour and margins.</p></li><li><p>2</p><h3>Preview live</h3><p>See an exact, true-to-scale preview update as you change settings — what you see is what prints.</p></li><li><p>3</p><h3>Download &amp; print</h3><p>Export a clean PDF (or PNG), then print at 100% scale for accurate grids every time.</p></li><!--]--></ol></section><section><h2>Supported graph paper sizes</h2><p> Every graph paper template generates across the full ISO A/B/C series and US/Imperial sizes. </p><div><!--[--><div><h3>US / Imperial</h3><ul><!--[--><li><span>US Letter</span><span>215.9 × 279.4 mm</span></li><li><span>US Legal</span><span>215.9 × 355.6 mm</span></li><li><span>Tabloid (Ledger)</span><span>279.4 × 431.8 mm</span></li><li><span>Executive</span><span>184.15 × 266.7 mm</span></li><li><span>Junior Legal</span><span>127 × 203.2 mm</span></li><li><span>Half Letter</span><span>139.7 × 215.9 mm</span></li><li><span>ANSI C</span><span>431.8 × 558.8 mm</span></li><li><span>ANSI D</span><span>558.8 × 863.6 mm</span></li><li><span>ANSI E</span><span>863.6 × 1117.6 mm</span></li><li><span>Arch A</span><span>228.6 × 304.8 mm</span></li><li><span>Arch B</span><span>304.8 × 457.2 mm</span></li><li><span>Arch C</span><span>457.2 × 609.6 mm</span></li><li><span>Arch D</span><span>609.6 × 914.4 mm</span></li><li><span>Arch E</span><span>914.4 × 1219.2 mm</span></li><!--]--></ul></div><div><h3>ISO A Series</h3><ul><!--[--><li><span>A0</span><span>841 × 1189 mm</span></li><li><span>A1</span><span>594 × 841 mm</span></li><li><span>A2</span><span>420 × 594 mm</span></li><li><span>A3</span><span>297 × 420 mm</span></li><li><span>A4</span><span>210 × 297 mm</span></li><li><span>A5</span><span>148 × 210 mm</span></li><li><span>A6</span><span>105 × 148 mm</span></li><li><span>A7</span><span>74 × 105 mm</span></li><li><span>A8</span><span>52 × 74 mm</span></li><li><span>A9</span><span>37 × 52 mm</span></li><li><span>A10</span><span>26 × 37 mm</span></li><!--]--></ul></div><div><h3>ISO B Series</h3><ul><!--[--><li><span>B0</span><span>1000 × 1414 mm</span></li><li><span>B1</span><span>707 × 1000 mm</span></li><li><span>B2</span><span>500 × 707 mm</span></li><li><span>B3</span><span>353 × 500 mm</span></li><li><span>B4</span><span>250 × 353 mm</span></li><li><span>B5</span><span>176 × 250 mm</span></li><li><span>B6</span><span>125 × 176 mm</span></li><li><span>B7</span><span>88 × 125 mm</span></li><li><span>B8</span><span>62 × 88 mm</span></li><li><span>B9</span><span>44 × 62 mm</span></li><li><span>B10</span><span>31 × 44 mm</span></li><!--]--></ul></div><div><h3>ISO C Series</h3><ul><!--[--><li><span>C0</span><span>917 × 1297 mm</span></li><li><span>C1</span><span>648 × 917 mm</span></li><li><span>C2</span><span>458 × 648 mm</span></li><li><span>C3</span><span>324 × 458 mm</span></li><li><span>C4</span><span>229 × 324 mm</span></li><li><span>C5</span><span>162 × 229 mm</span></li><li><span>C6</span><span>114 × 162 mm</span></li><li><span>C7</span><span>81 × 114 mm</span></li><li><span>C8</span><span>57 × 81 mm</span></li><li><span>C9</span><span>40 × 57 mm</span></li><li><span>C10</span><span>28 × 40 mm</span></li><!--]--></ul></div><!--]--></div></section><section><h2>Graph paper: questions &amp; answers</h2><div><!--[--><details><summary>What is graph paper? </summary><p>Graph paper — also called grid paper or squared paper — is paper printed with an even grid of squares that helps you draw to scale, plot data and keep work neat. FreeGraphPaper turns any grid into a clean, print-ready PDF.</p></details><details><summary>Is the printable graph paper free? </summary><p>Yes. Every graph paper PDF here is completely free — no login, no sign-up and no watermark. Download as many sheets as you like.</p></details><details><summary>How do I print graph paper at the right size? </summary><p>Download the PDF and print at 100% scale (turn off “fit to page”) so a 5 mm or 1/4 inch grid measures exactly right on paper.</p></details><details><summary>What graph paper sizes and spacings can I download? </summary><p>Popular options include 5 mm, 1 cm, 1/8 inch and 1/4 inch graph paper on A4, US Letter and the full ISO A/B/C range — plus dot grid, isometric, hexagon and lined paper.</p></details><!--]--></div></section></div></div>",
