    "text": "<div><div><div><p></p><h2><span>Intelligence</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2>Benchmarks</h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Openness Index</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Intelligence Index Comparisons</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Token Use</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Cost</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Context Window</span></h2><p></p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Speed</span></h2><p></p><p>Measured by Output Speed (tokens per second)</p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Latency</span></h2><p></p><p>Measured by Time (seconds) to First Token</p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>End-to-End Response Time</span></h2><p></p><p>Seconds to output 500 tokens, calculated based on time to first token, 'thinking' time for reasoning models, and output speed</p></div><div><p></p><h2><span>Model Size (Open Weights Models Only)</span></h2><p></p></div></div><section><div><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p>Common questions about GLM-5.2 (max)</p></div><div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) was released on June 16, 2026.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) was created by Z AI.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) scores 53 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, placing it well above average among other open weight models of similar size (median: 27).</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) generates output at 152.2 tokens per second (based on the median across providers serving the model), which is well above average compared to other open weight models of similar size (median: 66.2 t/s).</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) has a time to first token (TTFT) of 1.39s (based on the median across providers serving the model), which is very competitive compared to other open weight models of similar size (median: 1.96s).</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) costs $1.40 per 1M input tokens (at the higher end, median: $0.57) and $4.40 per 1M output tokens (at the higher end, median: $2.20), based on the median across providers serving the model.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) costs $1.40 per 1M input tokens and $4.40 per 1M output tokens (based on the median across providers serving the model). For a blended rate (7:2:1 cache hit/input/output ratio), this is $0.88 per 1M tokens. Pricing may vary by provider.<!-- --> Compare provider pricing</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>When evaluated on the Intelligence Index, GLM-5.2 (max) generated 140M output tokens, which is somewhat higher than average compared to other open weight models of similar size (median: 100M).</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>Yes, GLM-5.2 (max) is a reasoning model. It uses extended thinking or chain-of-thought reasoning to work through complex problems before providing an answer.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) supports text input.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) supports text output.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>No, GLM-5.2 (max) does not support image input. It can only process text.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>No, GLM-5.2 (max) is not multimodal. It only supports text input.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) has a context window of 1.0M tokens. This determines how much text and conversation history the model can process in a single request.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>Yes, GLM-5.2 (max) is open weights. The model weights are publicly available and can be downloaded for self-hosting.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) has 753 billion parameters (40 billion active).</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) is a Mixture of Experts (MoE) model with 753 billion total parameters, but only 40 billion active parameters are used during inference.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) is released under the Mit license. This license allows commercial use.<!-- --> View license</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) achieves a score of 53 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index. This composite benchmark evaluates models across reasoning, knowledge, mathematics, and coding.</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>Yes, GLM-5.2 (max) is available via API through 18 providers.<!-- --> Compare API providers</p></div></div><div><h3></h3><div><p>GLM-5.2 (max) is available through 18 API providers.<!-- --> Compare providers</p></div></div></div></section></div>",
