    "text": "<div><!-- NAV --><!-- Blueprint background: construction grid (always visible) + floating\n         squares (hidden on mobile). Rotated + scaled to feel like a drafting\n         sheet behind the hero. --><!-- HERO --><div><p>Flue 2.0 — Introducing Agent Hooks→</p><p>Build durable AI agents with Flue's programmable TypeScript harness. Write once, deploy anywhere, use any LLM.</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>“</span><span>Read https://flueframework.com/start.md then help create my first agent...<span>”</span></span></span><span><span>✓</span><span>!</span><span>Copied — now paste that into your coding agent for a guided walkthrough!</span><span>Could not copy prompt</span></span></span></span></p></div></div><dialog></dialog><!-- Hero code snippet, sitting astride the white → gray section break.\n\n         Background gradient hard-cuts at the vertical midpoint so the snippet\n         card visually straddles both hero (white) and body (gray) sections. --><div><!-- Code block chrome: filename (left) + run modes (right). --><div><p><span>agents/assistant.ts</span></p><div><!-- CLI agent interaction mode --><p><span>flue run ./agents/assistant.ts</span></p><!-- HTTP agent interaction mode --><p><span>POST /agents/assistant/:id</span></p></div></div><pre><code><span><span>export</span><span> function</span><span> MyAssistant</span><span>() {</span></span>\n<span><span>  const</span><span> [</span><span>count</span><span>, </span><span>setCount</span><span>] </span><span>=</span><span> usePersistentState</span><span>(</span><span>'count'</span><span>, </span><span>0</span><span>);</span></span>\n<span><span>  useAgentStart</span><span>(() </span><span>=&gt;</span><span> setCount</span><span>((</span><span>n</span><span>) </span><span>=&gt;</span><span> n </span><span>+</span><span> 1</span><span>));</span></span>\n<span><span>  useModel</span><span>(</span><span>'moonshot/kimi-k2'</span><span>);</span></span>\n<span><span>  return</span><span> `You are a helpful assistant. This conversation has ${</span><span>count</span><span>} messages.`</span><span>;</span></span>\n<span><span>}</span></span></code></pre></div><!-- Body sections — off-white background wraps everything below the hero. --><div><div><h2>Powered by Pi, the open agent harness.</h2><p>Flue is powered by Pi, the trusted agent harness used by OpenClaw and millions worldwide. Pi gives you the tools you need to unlock real agent autonomy, moving beyond simple chatbots.</p><p>Pi is the core of our open tech stack including Durable Streams, Vite, and a flexible Sandbox API. Deploy Flue anywhere with confidence.</p></div><div><div><div><h2>Durability. Recovery. It's all handled for you.</h2><p>Agents can’t die when the server goes down. Flue records every session in a durable stream, then safely resumes interrupted work when the runtime comes back online. Run one agent or a multi-agent swarm on the same durable foundation.</p><ul><li>Accepted work is never lost</li><li>Interrupted sessions resume automatically</li><li>Clients reconnect without starting over</li></ul></div><div><p><span>0 agents online</span></p></div></div><div><h2>Bring the stack you already love.</h2><p>Explore our ecosystem →</p></div></div><div><div><h2>Features</h2><p>Build agents that can safely take action, maintain continuity, and connect to the systems where work already happens.</p></div><p>AgentsBuild agents that can keep context across conversations and events as they autonomously work toward a goal. Each one is durable, stateful, and addressable over HTTP.WorkflowsAgents are just functions. Script them with flue run and the SDK — locally, in CI, or from your own backend — or orchestrate them with Cloudflare Workflows, Inngest, and more.SandboxesA secure environment where agents run commands, edit files, and do real work.Persistent StateWrite data on each agent and update its capabilities as state changes.SubagentsDefine specialized roles and let your agent delegate work to the right expert.ToolsAgents call APIs, query data, and make changes — using the code you define.SkillsPackage expertise that agents load whenever a task needs guidance.MCP ServersConnect agents to thousands of tools through the open Model Context Protocol.Durable ExecutionWork survives crashes, restarts, and deploys — sessions resume automatically.ObservabilityExport session traces to OpenTelemetry, Braintrust, Sentry, or your own observer.ChatConnect agents to where work happens — Slack, Teams, Discord, GitHub, and more.Explore the docsLearn how to build, run, and deploy production-ready agents with Flue.Read the docs →</p></div></div><!-- end off-white wrapper --></div>",
