    "url": "https://wccftech.com/grab-this-radeon-rx-9070-for-just-629-before-the-price-climbs-back-to-750/",
    "text": "<div><div>\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<p>This is a rare chance to buy the GPU for a good price as you will hardly find it for less than $700.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Radeon RX 9070 Sells for Nearly $700, but the ASUS Prime Radeon RX 9070 is Currently Sitting at Just $629 on Amazon</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If the recent GPU price hikes scared you, then this deal is for you. We spend a lot of time searching for amazing hardware deals on a daily basis, and today we got an amazing GPU deal on Amazon. This will be especially great if you were waiting to upgrade your GPU but couldn't get your hands on one due to insanely high prices. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>This is the Radeon RX 9070 16 GB GPU that was launched last year for $549. Thanks to RAMpocalypse, you can no longer find it for around $600, let alone at MSRP, as memory prices have pushed GPU prices up by at least 40% in the last 10 months. This is why the Radeon RX 9070 sits at around $700 at most retailers, while its bigger sibling is easily touching $800. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>This particular deal is available on Amazon and is a limited time deal, which means it can end anytime. For just $629, you will get this amazing triple-fan ASUS Prime Radeon RX 9070 16 GB OC card, which usually sells for $750. We checked its price history and $649 was its lowest price tag in the last three months. This makes $629 a terrific price tag, considering you get competitive performance to RTX 5070 for less. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Moreover, the GPU gives you a good 16 GB VRAM capacity, which will keep your rig future proof for a while. The Radeon RX 9070 is one of the fastest mid-range graphics card, based on the RDNA 4 architecture. The GPU uses the NAVI 48 die and brings 3584 Stream Processors, 16 GB GDDR6 VRAM through a 256-bit bus, and can boost up to 2610 MHz on this particular design.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Buy ASUS Prime Radeon RX 9070 16 GB OC at $629 from Amazon</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\tIf you buy something from a Amazon affiliate link, Wccftech may earn a commission. See our ethics statement.\n\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<strong>About the author: </strong> Sarfraz Khan is a hardware reporter with a focus on PC components and the builder community. With years of experience writing about PC hardware and laptops, his work has been featured on several reputable technology publications. \n\nSarfraz's hands-on experience is demonstrated through his first-person accounts of using and comparing different hardware configurations, providing practical and relatable insights for everyday users. His technical analysis is respected by peers in the enthusiast community and has been cited by specialized hardware sites such as Germany's Igor's Lab.\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<p>\n\t\t\t\tFollow Wccftech on Google to get more of our news coverage in your feeds.\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\t</div><p>Read all comments on Grab This Radeon RX 9070 For Just $629 Before The Price Climbs Back To $750\n\t\n</p></div>",
