    "category": "Technology",
    "title": "Simon Willison’s Weblog",
    "url": "https://simonwillison.net/guides/agentic-engineering-patterns/",
    "text": "<div><div>\n\n\n\n\n<h2>Agentic Engineering Patterns</h2>\n\n<p>Patterns for getting the best results out of coding agents like Claude Code and OpenAI Codex. See my introduction for more on this project.</p>\n\n<ol>\n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Principles</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              What is agentic engineering?\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Agentic engineering</li>\n                \n                <li>Isn't this just vibe coding?</li>\n                \n                <li>About this guide</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Writing code is cheap now\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Good code still has a cost</li>\n                \n                <li>We need to build new habits</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Hoard things you know how to do\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Recombining things from your hoard</li>\n                \n                <li>Coding agents make this even more powerful</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              AI should help us produce better code\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Avoiding taking on technical debt</li>\n                \n                <li>Coding agents can handle these for us</li>\n                \n                <li>AI tools let us consider more options</li>\n                \n                <li>Embrace the compound engineering loop</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Anti-patterns: things to avoid\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Inflicting unreviewed code on collaborators</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Working with coding agents</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              How coding agents work\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Large Language Models</li>\n                \n                <li>Chat templated prompts</li>\n                \n                <li>Token caching</li>\n                \n                <li>Calling tools</li>\n                \n                <li>The system prompt</li>\n                \n                <li>Reasoning</li>\n                \n                <li>LLM + system prompt + tools in a loop</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Using Git with coding agents\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Git essentials</li>\n                \n                <li>Core concepts and prompts</li>\n                \n                <li>Rewriting history</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Subagents\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Claude Code’s Explore subagent</li>\n                \n                <li>Parallel subagents</li>\n                \n                <li>Specialist subagents</li>\n                \n                <li>Official documentation</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Testing and QA</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              Red/green TDD\n              \n              \n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              First run the tests\n              \n              \n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Agentic manual testing\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Mechanisms for agentic manual testing</li>\n                \n                <li>Using browser automation for web UIs</li>\n                \n                <li>Have them take notes with Showboat</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Understanding code</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              Linear walkthroughs\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>An example using Showboat and Present</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Interactive explanations\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Understanding word clouds</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Annotated prompts</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              GIF optimization tool using WebAssembly and Gifsicle\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>The follow-up prompts</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n            <li>\n              Adding a new content type to my blog-to-newsletter tool\n              \n              \n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n    \n      <li>\n        <strong>Appendix</strong>\n        <ol>\n          \n            <li>\n              Prompts I use\n              \n              \n              \n              <ul>\n                \n                <li>Artifacts</li>\n                \n                <li>Proofreader</li>\n                \n                <li>Alt text</li>\n                \n                <li>Podcast highlights</li>\n                \n              </ul>\n              \n              \n            </li>\n          \n        </ol>\n      </li>\n    \n  \n</ol>\n\n\n\n</div></div>",
