    "title": "Fading Maize | 2001 to 2026",
    "url": "https://www.fadingmaize.com",
    "text": "<div><div><div><p>Ripon College Band, AI‑Revived 25 Years Later</p><p>Original songs from a Ripon College band, carried from a 2001 dorm-room archive into a 2026 AI-assisted revival.</p><p>Explore The MusicEnter 2001</p></div><div><div><p>The premise</p><h2>Not An AI Band. A Real Band With Unfinished Reach.</h2></div><div><p>Charlie Saponara wrote the songs. Jacob Graf joined on drums after arriving at Ripon College. Brad Mott was part of the original lineup. The recordings, lyrics, photos, and history are real Fading Maize artifacts.</p><p>The 2026 project is the second chance: AI-assisted production, design, video, artwork, and release strategy used openly to make the songs feel as big as they felt back then.</p><p>The whole revival runs on five public principles: consent, authorship, provenance, nothing erased, nobody displaced. The original recordings stay streaming beside the new versions, so the receipts are always one tap away.</p><p>How The Revival Works</p></div></div><div><div><div><p>Music</p><h2>Hear The Difference.</h2></div><div><p>Play the original archive recording, then hop straight to the 2026 Reimagined Edition mid-song and back again. The full music page collects release context, Bandcamp support links, streaming destinations, and credits.</p><p>View Full Music Page</p></div></div><div><div><article><div><p><span>What's Happened to You?</span></p><p>Track one of the first album, and the first song to go fully 2026.</p></div></article><article><div><p><span>Girl Just Like Mary Tyler Moore</span></p><p>The fan-favorite archive oddity, finally given a finished version.</p></div></article></div><div><div><p>Full Versions</p><h3>Follow, Stream, Or Support Directly.</h3></div><p>Support on BandcampBandcampStream on SpotifySpotifyListen on Apple MusicApple MusicPlay on YouTube MusicYouTube MusicPlay on Amazon MusicAmazon Music</p></div></div><div><article><div><p><img></p><p><img></p></div><div><p>2001<!-- --> to <!-- -->2026</p><h3>Release These Words</h3><p>Original album archive, then <!-- -->Reimagined Edition<!-- -->.</p></div></article><article><div><p><img></p><p><img></p></div><div><p>2002<!-- --> to <!-- -->2026</p><h3>Risk Is Everything</h3><p>Original album archive, then <!-- -->Reimagined Edition<!-- -->.</p></div></article><article><div><p><img></p><p><img></p></div><div><p>2003<!-- --> to <!-- -->2026</p><h3>The Recovery Process</h3><p>Original album archive, then <!-- -->Reimagined Edition<!-- -->.</p></div></article></div></div><div><div><p>Archive</p><h2>The Old Site Is Part Of The Art.</h2><p>A curated entry point for shows, recording photos, videos, flyers, and recovered artifacts, with the original 2001 site preserved as part of the experience.</p><p>Open Full Archive</p></div><p>FrontPage time capsuleOriginal 2001 WebsiteThe old site preserved as an intentionally awkward, honest archive.Risk Is EverythingDorm-Room RecordingPhotos from the room where the original college recordings came together.Ripon CollegeFirst ShowsGreat Hall, Wisconsin shows, and the beginning of the audience memory.</p><div><p>From the shelves</p></div></div><div><div><p>Timeline</p><h2>From Dorm Room To Launch Plan.</h2></div><ol><li><time>2000</time><div><p><strong>Charlie and Brad start Fading Maize</strong></p><p>The acoustic college-band idea begins before Jacob arrives at Ripon.</p></div></li><li><time>2001</time><div><p><strong>Jacob joins at Ripon College</strong></p><p>Charlie finds Jacob on campus and asks him to join on drums and backing vocals.</p></div></li><li><time>2002</time><div><p><strong>Dorm-room recordings and Wisconsin shows</strong></p><p>The band records in Charlie's room and plays around Ripon, Oshkosh, and Wisconsin.</p></div></li><li><time>2025</time><div><p><strong>The old site comes back online</strong></p><p>Jacob buys fadingmaize.com back and relaunches the 2001 site in October 2025.</p></div></li><li><time>2026</time><div><p><strong>The Reimagined Editions arrive</strong></p><p>All three original albums return to streaming beside their full 2026 AI-assisted revivals.</p></div></li></ol></div><div><div><div><p>The people</p><h2>The Humans Stay In The Credits.</h2></div><p>Fading Maize was real before the revival tools existed. The archive, the authorship, and the 2026 work are presented as connected history without blurring who is actively shaping what.</p></div><div><article><p><img></p><div><p><span>Songs and voice</span><span>Active creative voice</span></p><div><p>Acoustic guitar, lead vocals, songwriter</p><h3><span>Charlie (Chuck)</span><span>Saponara</span></h3></div><div><p>Original songwriter and lead voice behind the Fading Maize catalog.</p><p>The revival keeps Charlie's authorship at the center while he provides feedback, approvals, and creative tweaks for the new versions.</p></div></div></article><article><p><img></p><div><p><span>Rhythm and rebuild</span><span>Revival lead</span></p><div><p>Drums, backing vocals</p><h3><span>Jacob Graf</span></h3></div><div><p>Original-era drummer carrying the archive into the 2026 release cycle.</p><p>Jacob is handling the concept, site build, AI-assisted workflow, platform setup, launch system, and ongoing creative operations.</p></div></div></article><article><p><img></p><div><p><span>Original lineup</span><span>Historical credit</span></p><div><p>Acoustic guitar, backing vocals</p><h3><span>Brad Mott</span></h3></div><div><p>Historical member credited for original-era guitar and backing vocal contributions.</p><p>The 2026 story does not present Brad as part of the active revival unless he chooses to participate.</p></div></div></article></div></div><div><div><p>Still coming</p><h2>What Comes Online Next.</h2></div><div><p><strong>More before-and-after pairs</strong><span>Additional songs join the comparison player as archive clips are prepared.</span></p><p><strong>Recovered video and photo archive</strong><span>Original-era show footage, dorm-room recordings, and photo sets as they are cleaned up.</span></p><p><strong>Direct-to-fan extras</strong><span>Bandcamp bonus material and merch experiments as the audience grows.</span></p><p>Understand The 2026 Revival</p></div></div></div></div>",
