    "id": "tech_hn_47195123",
    "source": "HackerNews (Distributed)",
    "category": "Technology",
    "title": "Now I Get It! · Scientific articles, explained.",
    "url": "https://nowigetit.us",
    "text": "<div>\n  \n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       Sticky header.\n       Auth state (sign-in vs profile menu) is wired by auth-ui.js\n       via the existing site convention. Header CTA points to /index.html\n       which is the current upload page; change to /upload.html when the\n       dedicated upload page ships.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  \n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       HERO\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <section>\n    <img>\n    \n    <p>Scientific articles, explained.</p>\n    <p>Upload a scientific PDF and get back a shareable, interactive web page that explains it in plain language.</p>\n    <p>Sign In\n      Read a featured one ↗\n    </p>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- BEFORE / AFTER VIDEO DEMO — assets at backend/static/{before,after}.mp4 -->\n  <div>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><span></span><span>Before · PDF</span>\n        </p>\n        <video>\n          <source>\n          <!-- Optional second source — add if you encode a .webm:\n          <source src=\"landing/before.webm\" type=\"video/webm\"> -->\n        </video>\n        <p>15 pages of two-column jargon</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <p><span>translate</span>\n        <span>→</span>\n      </p>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><span></span><span>After · Now I Get It!</span>\n        </p>\n        <video>\n          <source>\n          <!-- <source src=\"landing/after.webm\" type=\"video/webm\"> -->\n        </video>\n        <p>Same paper. You actually get it.</p>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       WHY THIS EXISTS — the moral / cultural case\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <div>\n        <p>2,500,000<span>+</span></p>\n        <p>scientific papers published every year — all of them written for other scientists.</p>\n        \n        <p>~ 40<span>%</span></p>\n        <p>of research funded with public money — paid for by the same taxpayers who can't read the results.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Why this exists</span></p><h2>Scientific breakthroughs happen every day. <em>Very few people can understand them.</em></h2>\n        <p>Scientific papers are written for other scientists. This leaves out everyone else: the curious, the students, the journalists, the kids, the experts in adjacent fields, the taxpayers who paid for the research.</p>\n        <p>The result is a widening cultural divide around science — at exactly the moment we need the opposite. <strong>Now I Get It! exists to close it, one paper at a time.</strong></p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       THREE READING MODES\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Three modes</span></p><h2>Same paper. Translated for different audiences.</h2>\n        <p>Pick the lens before you translate. Or run it more than once — every translation is a separate page in your gallery.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <p><span>Native</span>\n          <span>For a technical audience</span></p><p>Same structure and terminology as the paper, just reinterpreted for web. Use when you want a page that complements the original paper.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <p><span>Non-technical</span>\n          <span>For an intelligent audience</span></p><p>Jargon replaced. Context added. Concepts explained in plain language. The default for curious readers without the field background. Cross-disciplinary reading made fast.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <p><span>Kid-friendly</span>\n          <span>For curious little ones</span></p><p>The paper as a story. Narrative voice, illustrations, fun designs. Great for kids of all ages. Parents and teachers love this one.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       PUBLIC GALLERY CAROUSEL — preserved from existing index.html.\n       Pulls from /api/library with the same JS pattern.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  \n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       FEATURED COLLECTIONS — preserved from existing index.html.\n       Pulls from /api/public/categories.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <p><span>Featured Collections</span></p><h2>Hand-picked papers, completely re-imagined.</h2>\n      <p>Come see some of our favorites.</p>\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       USE CASES — drawn from real testing observations\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Uses for Now I Get It!</span></p><h2>Everyone is curious about science.</h2>\n        <p>People use Now I Get It! in many fascinating ways.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Personal interest</h3>\n          <p>You saw a paper on Twitter. You want to actually understand it.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Cross-field reading</h3>\n          <p>Rapid orientation in an unfamiliar field. Skim three papers in the time it took to skim one.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Kids</h3>\n          <p>Introduce a child to amazing science in language they can actually follow.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Companion pages</h3>\n          <p>Professors and labs publishing readable web versions of their own papers.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Due diligence</h3>\n          <p>VCs and analysts getting through a stack of technical papers without a PhD in every field.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Internal explainers</h3>\n          <p>Engineers translating dense architecture papers to share with teammates.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Translation between languages</h3>\n          <p>Convert an English paper into a Spanish web page — or any other language pair.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       HOW IT WORKS\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <section>\n    <div>\n      <p><span>How it works</span></p><h2>Three steps. Yours forever.</h2>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        <p>01</p>\n        <h3>Upload your PDF</h3>\n        <p>Drop any scientific paper — arXiv, bioRxiv, a journal PDF, your lab's preprint, a doctoral thesis. We handle papers up to about 20 MB.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <p>02</p>\n        <h3>We translate it</h3>\n        <p>Pick a reading mode — Native, Non-technical, or Kid-friendly. You have the option of choosing a theme and can even add custom instructions.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <p>03</p>\n        <h3>Read. Edit. Share.</h3>\n        <p>Your translation lands in your private gallery. From there you can view it, share it, add tags, and even make edits to text and fomulas.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       PRIVACY / GALLERY\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Your gallery</span></p><h2>Private by default. Public by choice.</h2>\n        <p>Every translation you create lands in your personal gallery, visible only to you. Share when you want — not before.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Private by default</h3>\n          <p>Every translation lands in your personal gallery, visible only to you.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Share via link</h3>\n          <p>Flip a toggle to make any translation reachable by URL. Nothing else changes.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Publish</h3>\n          <p>Flip another toggle to feature it in the Public Gallery for everyone.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Organize with tags</h3>\n          <p>Stack tags by field, by mode, by audience, by project. Filter with OR / AND.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Editable Results</h3>\n          <p>Text and formulas are editable inline on any translation you own.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       PRICING — credit packs\n       Prices/credits mirror what's currently on /credits.html — confirm\n       and adjust if the live numbers have moved.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <section>\n    <div>\n      <p><span>Purchase Credits</span></p><h2>Pay only when you translate.</h2>\n      <p>Most papers can be translated with one credit. Credits never expire. No subscription required!</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><img></p><p>Single</p>\n        <p><span>1</span><span>credit</span></p>\n        <p>$3.00</p>\n        <p>$3.00/credit</p>\n        <p>Buy\n      </p></div>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><img></p><p>Starter</p>\n        <p><span>5</span><span>credits</span></p>\n        <p>$12.50</p>\n        <p>$2.50/credit</p>\n        <p>Save 17%</p>\n        <p>Buy\n      </p></div>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Popular</span>\n        <img></p><p>Explorer</p>\n        <p><span>15</span><span>credits</span></p>\n        <p>$35.00</p>\n        <p>$2.33/credit</p>\n        <p>Save 22%</p>\n        <p>Buy\n      </p></div>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><img></p><p>Scholar</p>\n        <p><span>50</span><span>credits</span></p>\n        <p>$105.00</p>\n        <p>$2.10/credit</p>\n        <p>Save 30%</p>\n        <p>Buy\n      </p></div>\n    </div>\n    <p>All purchases are final. Credits are non-refundable, non-transferable, and do not expire. </p>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       FAQ TEASER — keep short, link to the full /faq.html\n       Answers were pulled from the live FAQ; adjust if the canonical\n       text has changed.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><span>Common questions</span></p><h2>Stuff people ask.</h2>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <details>\n          <summary>\n            <span>What does it cost?</span>\n            <span></span>\n          </summary>\n          <p>A single credit costs $3. Save money by purchasing credit packs. No subscription required! You can process as many or as few papers as you like.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>\n            <span>Can I restrict who sees the result?</span>\n            <span></span>\n          </summary>\n          <p>Yes — all translations are private by default. They sit in your personal gallery. From there you can make a page shareable via link or fully public (it will appear in the Public Gallery). Note: we take copyright seriously. Don't share translations from copyrighted works you don't own the rights to.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>\n            <span>Can I edit the output?</span>\n            <span></span>\n          </summary>\n          <p>Yes. Text and formulas (KaTeX-rendered) are editable on any translation you own. Charts and diagrams are drawn by code at load time — to change one, re-process the PDF. You can also add custom instructions before translating.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>\n            <span>What kinds of papers work?</span>\n            <span></span>\n          </summary>\n          <p>We've translated thousands of papers. Some up to several hundred pages long and many in languages other than English. When you upload a paper, we calculate the number of credits required to translate it and ask for your approval before we start.</p>\n        </details>\n        <details>\n          <summary>\n            <span>Where can I find scientific papers?</span>\n            <span></span>\n          </summary>\n          <p>Great question! You can find scientific papers on the web in many places. Our favorites are open access platforms like arXiv and bioRxiv. You can also find papers in journals like PLOS and APS.</p>\n        </details>        \n      </div>\n      <p>Read the full FAQ →\n    </p></div>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       FINAL CTA\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  <section>\n    <img>\n    <h2>Translate some amazing science today.</h2>\n    Sign In\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       Site-standard script load order — matches index.html\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       Auth-aware CTAs (issue #387):\n       \"Translate a paper\" links bounce signed-out users to a sign-in form\n       — a dark pattern. Show \"Sign In\" (opens the sign-in modal) until the\n       user is authenticated; only then reveal \"Translate a paper\" → upload.\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  \n\n  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n       Landing-page glue:\n       1. Maintenance banner (same convention as index.html)\n       2. Public Gallery carousel: lazy-loaded from /api/library\n       3. Featured Collections: loaded from /api/public/categories\n       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n  \n\n\n</div>",
    "score": 305,
    "date": "2026-02-28T13:29:36.000Z"
