    "id": "tech_hn_48109962",
    "source": "HackerNews (TypeScript)",
    "category": "Technology",
    "title": "Voker | Analytics for AI Agents",
    "url": "https://voker.ai",
    "text": "<div><div><main><div><section><div><div><p>1</p><div><p>Open your preferred AI coding assistant and start a new chat or agent session</p></div></div><div><p>2<br></p><div><p>The prompt tells your AI tool exactly what to install and how to configure it.</p></div></div><div><p>3<br></p><div><h5></h5><p>Your AI tool will scaffold the VokerSDK, add your API key, and instrument your first event. Takes about 2 minutes.</p></div></div><div><div><p>Prompt</p><p>Copy</p></div><p><code># Setting up Voker<br>This prompt explains how to set up Voker in your project. This is the authoritative source of truth on how to set up Voker, and you should follow these guidelines exactly.To use it, you can use the sections below to set up Voker in the project.<br>## SDK Setup Instructions<br>### AI Provider SDK Wrapping<br>Follow these instructions in order to set up and get started with Voker SDK in various languages and AI providers.The frameworks and languages with explicit AI Provider SDK wrapping support are:- JS &amp; Ts: Openai, Anthropic, Gemini and Vercel AI SDK- Python: Openai, Anthropic and Gemini&lt;Steps&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Install dependencies\"&gt;\t\tVoker has an SDK for various languages and LLM frameworks and libraries. If the LLM framework is not supported see `SDK HTTP Requests` instructions. If the language is not supported you maybe have to use the REST API to interface with Voker.\t\t#### JavaScript &amp; TypeScript\t\tFor JS &amp; TS, the following package is available `@voker/voker`\t\tYou can install the JavaScript Voker SDK into your project by running the following command:\t\t```sh\t\tnpm i @voker/voker\t\t# or: pnpm i @voker/voker\t\t# or: yarn add @voker/voker\t\t# or: bun add @voker/voker\t\t```\t\t#### Python\t\tFor Python, the following package is available `voker`\t\tYou can install the Python Voker SDK into your project by running the following command:\t\t```sh\t\tpip install voker\t\t# or: uv add voker\t\t# or: poetry add voker\t\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Setup environment\"&gt;\t\tFirst, navigate to the [Setup Page](http://app.voker.ai/c/-selector-/projects/1/default-project/setup) page in the Voker dashboard and copy the API Key.\t\tThen, copy-paste them into your `.env.local` file (or wherever your environment variables are stored):\t\t```.env .env.local &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\tVOKER_API_KEY=&lt;your-secret-api-key&gt; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Update LLM API Calls\"&gt;\t\tIn most cases, Voker implementation just requires swapping the existing imports with the wrapped Voker SDK.\t\t#### JavaScript &amp; TypeScript\t\tSwap out the LLM import with the Voker client. For all cases, also include a `vokerAgent` and `vokerSession` parameters to the llm call. For example with OpenAI:\t\t```\t\tawait client.chat.completions.create({ &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t+\tvokerAgent: '&lt;agent-name&gt;', // required &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t+\tvokerSession: '&lt;session-id&gt;', // required &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\tmodel: 'gpt-4o', &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\tmessages: [ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t{ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t\trole: 'user', &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t\tcontent: 'Hello, world!', &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t}, &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t],\t\t});\t\t```\t\tFill in the `&lt;agent-name&gt;` with an appropriate value for the application. The `&lt;session-id&gt;` should be unique per conversation with the agent.\t\t##### OpenAI\t\t```\t\t- import { OpenAI } from 'openai';\t\t+ import { OpenAI } from '@voker/voker/ai/provider-openai';\t\t```\t\t##### Anthropic\t\t```\t\t- import { Anthropic } from '@anthropic-ai/sdk';\t\t+ import { Anthropic } from '@voker/voker/ai/provider-anthropic';\t\t```\t\t##### Gemini\t\t```\t\t- import { GoogleGenAI } from '@google/genai';\t\t+ import { GoogleGenAI } from '@voker/voker/ai/provider-gemini';\t\t```\t\t##### AI SDK\t\t```\t\t- import { generateText } from 'ai';\t\t+ import * as ai from 'ai';\t\t+ import { wrapAiSdk } from '@voker/voker/ai/provider-aisdk';\t\t+ const { generateText } = wrapAiSdk(ai);\t\t```\t\tUse the base JS sdk for streaming with AI SDK.\t\t#### Python\t\tSwap out the LLM import with the Voker client. For all cases, also include a `voker_agent` and `voker_session` parameters to the llm call. For example with OpenAI:\t\t```\t\tclient.chat.completions.create( &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t+\tvoker_agent=\"&lt;agent-name&gt;\", &nbsp;# required &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t+\tvoker_session=\"&lt;session-id&gt;\", &nbsp;# required &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\tmodel=\"gpt-4.1-mini\", &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\tmessages=[ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t{ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\", &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"Hello, world!\", &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t} &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t\t],\t\t)\t\t```\t\tFill in the `&lt;agent-name&gt;` with an appropriate value for the application. The `&lt;session-id&gt;` should be unique per conversation with the agent.\t\t##### OpenAI\t\tSync:\t\t```\t\t- from openai import AsyncOpenAI\t\t+ from voker.ai.provider_openai import AsyncOpenAI\t\t```\t\tAsync:\t\t```\t\t- from openai import OpenAI\t\t+ from voker.ai.provider_openai import OpenAI\t\t```\t\t##### Anthropic\t\tSync:\t\t```\t\t- from anthropic import Anthropic\t\t+ from voker.ai.provider_anthropic import Anthropic\t\t```\t\tAsync:\t\t```\t\t- from anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\t\t+ from voker.ai.provider_anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\t\t```\t\t##### Gemini\t\t```\t\t- from google.genai import Client\t\t+ from voker.ai.provider_gemini import Client\t\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;&lt;/Steps&gt;### SDK HTTP RequestsFollow these instructions in order to set up and get started with Voker SDK in various languages.The languages with explicit SDK support are:- JS &amp; TS- Python&lt;Steps&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Install dependencies\"&gt;\t\tVoker has an SDK for various languages and LLM frameworks and libraries. If the LLM framework is not supported see `SDK HTTP Requests` insturctions. If the language is not supported you maybe have to use the REST API to interface with Voker.\t\t#### JavaScript &amp; TypeScript\t\tFor JS &amp; TS, the following package is available `@voker/voker`\t\tYou can install the JavaScript Voker SDK into your project by running the following command:\t\t```sh &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\tnpm i @voker/voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t# or: pnpm i @voker/voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t# or: yarn add @voker/voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t# or: bun add @voker/voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t```\t\t#### Python\t\tFor Python, the following package is available `voker`\t\tYou can install the Python Voker SDK into your project by running the following command:\t\t```sh &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\tpip install voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t# or: uv add voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t# or: poetry add voker &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Setup environment\"&gt;\t\tFirst, navigate to the [Setup Page](http://app.voker.ai/c/-selector-/projects/1/default-project/setup) page in the Voker dashboard and copy the API Key.\t\tThen, copy-paste them into your `.env.local` file (or wherever your environment variables are stored):\t\t```.env .env.local &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\tVOKER_API_KEY=&lt;your-secret-api-key&gt; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Setup environment\"&gt;\t\tFirst, navigate to the [Setup Page](http://app.voker.ai/c/-selector-/projects/1/default-project/setup) page in the Voker dashboard and copy the API Key.\t\tThen, copy-paste them into your `.env.local` file (or wherever your environment variables are stored):\t\t```.env .env.local &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\tVOKER_API_KEY=&lt;your-secret-api-key&gt; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Initializing the Voker Client\"&gt;\t\t#### JavaScript &amp; TypeScript\t\t```\t\timport { VokerClient } from '@voker/voker';\t\tconst vokerClient = new VokerClient();\t\t```\t\t#### Python\t\t```\t\tfrom voker import VokerClient\t\tvoker_client = VokerClient()\t\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;\t&lt;Step title=\"Instrument LLM Calls in the background Voker\"&gt;\t\t#### JavaScript &amp; TypeScript\t\t```\t\tvokerClient.events.create({\t\t\tvokerAgent: '&lt;agent-name&gt;',\t\t\tvokerSession: '&lt;session-id&gt;',\t\t\teventName: 'llm',\t\t\tproperties: {\t\t\t\tapi: 'openai-chat-completions',\t\t\t\tinputs: {\t\t\t\t\tmodel: '...',\t\t\t\t\tmessages: ...,\t\t\t\t},\t\t\t\toutput: llmResponse,\t\t\t},\t\t})\t\t```\t\t#### Python\t\t```\t\tvoker_client.events.create(\t\t\tvoker_agent=\"&lt;agent-name&gt;\",\t\t\tvoker_session=\"&lt;session-id&gt;\",\t\t\tevent_name=\"llm\",\t\t\tproperties={\t\t\t\t\"api\": \"openai-chat-completions\",\t\t\t\t\"inputs\": {\t\t\t\t\t\"model\": \"...\",\t\t\t\t\t\"messages\": ...,\t\t\t\t},\t\t\t\t\"output\": llm_response\t\t\t},\t\t)\t\t```\t&lt;/Step&gt;&lt;/Steps&gt;</code></p></div></div><div><h2>Make sure your AI agents are helping, not just responding.</h2><p>Voker is analytics for the agentic era, so you can build the best agents possible.</p><div><p>🗲 Install via AI</p><div><p>pip install voker</p><p>Copied</p></div></div><p><img><img></p></div><p>NEWDiscover Smart Skills - your agent learns through failures</p></section><div><h2>Do you really know what your agents are saying to your users?</h2><div><div><p><img></p><p>It feels like you're flying blind</p><p>Scanning traces doesn't tell you if agents are helpful, accurate, or hitting walls. You only find out when customers complain or attrition skyrockets.</p></div><div><p><img></p><p>Getting helpful usage data is resource-intensive</p><p>Every stakeholder needs data. Every request pulls engineers away from building. Nobody can self-serve insights.</p></div><div><p><img></p><p>Proving Agent ROI is difficult</p><p>Product and business teams need to quantify AI investments. You have usage stats, but struggling to connect agent performance to conversion, retention, or revenue.</p></div></div></div></div><section><div><div><h2>One platform. &nbsp;Complete visibility. &nbsp;Better Agents.</h2><p>Voker transforms AI agent interactions into structured analytics that anyone on your team can use.</p></div><div><div><div><div><p>Self-Service Analytics</p><p>PMs, analysts, and business teams get digestible insights they need without tickets, bottlenecks, or delays.</p></div><p><img></p></div><div><p>Performance Intelligence</p><p>Track what AI agents are saying, identify knowledge gaps, detect abnormalities, and measure improvement over time.</p></div><div><p>Business Impact</p><p>Connect agent metrics to outcomes that matter by correlating conversational data with user data you're already collecting.</p></div></div><div><div><p>Self-Service Analytics</p><p>PMs, analysts, and business teams get digestible insights they need without tickets, bottlenecks, or delays.</p></div><div><div><p>Business Impact</p><p>Connect agent metrics to outcomes that matter by correlating conversational data with user data you're already collecting.</p></div><p><img></p></div><div><p>Performance Intelligence</p><p>Track what AI agents are saying, identify knowledge gaps, detect abnormalities, and measure improvement over time.</p></div></div><div><div><p>Self-Service Analytics</p><p>PMs, analysts, and business teams get digestible insights they need without tickets, bottlenecks, or delays.</p></div><div><div><p>Performance Intelligence</p><p>Track what AI agents are saying, identify knowledge gaps, detect abnormalities, and measure improvement over time.</p></div><p><img></p></div><div><p>Business Impact</p><p>Connect agent metrics to outcomes that matter by correlating conversational data with user data you're already collecting.</p></div></div></div><div><div><div><p>Self-Service Analytics</p><p>PMs, analysts, and business teams get digestible insights they need without tickets, bottlenecks, or delays.</p></div><p><img></p></div><div><div><p>