    "text": "<div><div>\n    \n\n    <main>\n      <div>\n\n\n        <article>\n          \n          \n\n          <div>\n                <p>The results are in! Thank you all so much for your patience as we reviewed over 400 submissions for this challenge. </p>\n\n<p>We're going to jump right in because our full list of winners and runner-ups is quite long. Regardless of whether or not you were shortlisted, we hope you're proud of yourself for rising to the challenge. </p>\n\n\n<div>\n\n  \n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Congratulations To…\n</h2>\n\n<p>@georgekobaidze built Metal Birds Watch, a tool that allows you to track planes overhead without ever leaving your terminal. It’s a perfect showcase of how the Copilot CLI can help turn a unique hobbyist idea into a functional reality.</p>\n\n\n<div>\n  <p>Metal Birds Watch: Copilot CLI Helped Me Watch Planes Without Looking Up</p><div>\n      <p>GitHub Copilot CLI Challenge Submission\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Giorgi Kobaidze\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Feb 13\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          Metal Birds Watch: Copilot CLI Helped Me Watch Planes Without Looking Up\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #githubchallenge\n            #cli\n            #githubcopilot\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              50&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              17&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            11 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<p>@pengeszikra built RuStroke, a minimal vector drawing application. By utilizing GitHub Copilot CLI as a thinking partner and code modifier, Peter was able to build a complex geometry engine that can be plugged into other frontend or future drawing applications. </p>\n\n\n<div>\n  <p>Rustroke - WASM mini draw</p><div>\n      <p>GitHub Copilot CLI Challenge Submission\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Peter Vivo\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Feb 15\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          Rustroke - WASM mini draw\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #githubchallenge\n            #cli\n            #githubcopilot\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              17&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              5&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            4 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<p>@cturner8 developed BinMate, an app for managing binary installations from GitHub releases. BinMate provides an easy way to install, manage, and switch between different versions of command-line tools which makes the lives of developers (especially Linux users) easier. </p>\n\n\n<div>\n  <p>binmate - a binary version manager</p><div>\n      <p>GitHub Copilot CLI Challenge Submission\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              cameron turner\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Feb 15\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          binmate - a binary version manager\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #githubchallenge\n            #cli\n            #githubcopilot\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n  