    "title": "Congrats to the OpenClaw Challenge Winners!",
    "url": "https://dev.to/devteam/congrats-to-the-openclaw-challenge-winners-1lha",
    "text": "<div><div>\n    \n\n    <main>\n      <div>\n\n\n        <article>\n          \n          \n\n          <div>\n              <p>Hacking agents and power prediction tools</p>\n            <div>\n                <p>The results are in! We are thrilled to announce the winners of the OpenClaw Challenge.</p>\n\n<p>Over the past few weeks, you've been building, writing, and sharing your OpenClaw experiences with the community. Whether you were automating the mundane or tackling real-world infrastructure challenges, your submissions were a blast to review.</p>\n\n<p>Selecting six winners from this pool of submissions was no easy task. Let's give a round of applause to our winners!</p>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  🎉 Congratulations To…\n</h2>\n\n\n<div>\n\n  \n<h3>\n  \n  \n  OpenClaw in Action Winners\n</h3>\n\n\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@prema_ananda's WhiteHat is an autonomous ethical hacking agent that takes on the repetitive cycle of pentesting: scanning, reasoning, acting, and documenting, so you don't have to. A single SOUL.md file is what transforms the underlying LLM from a text generator into a methodical, principled penetration tester.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>Building WhiteHat: An Autonomous Ethical Hacking Agent with OpenClaw</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Prema Ananda\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 18\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          Building WhiteHat: An Autonomous Ethical Hacking Agent with OpenClaw\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #openclawchallenge\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              28&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              2&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            6 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@lewisawe built KPLC Sentinel, a WhatsApp-based agent that analyzes prepaid electricity token purchase history to predict when a user's power will run out before it actually does. The result is a practical, real-world automation that solves a frustrating problem for anyone on a prepaid electricity plan.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>I Made My WhatsApp Predict When My Electricity Will Run Out with Openclaw</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Lewis Sawe\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 25\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          I Made My WhatsApp Predict When My Electricity Will Run Out with Openclaw\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #openclawchallenge\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              8&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              1&nbsp;comment\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            8 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@jasmin used OpenClaw's persona files to build a multi-agent system where two AI agents can talk to each other with controlled, limited information. A markdown file acts as a privacy contract, determining exactly what each agent is and isn't allowed to reveal about its human.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>I Taught Two AIs What Not to Say About Their Humans</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Jasmin Virdi\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 26\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          I Taught Two AIs What Not to Say About Their Humans\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #openclawchallenge\n            #ai\n            #programming\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              30&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              28&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            4 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Wealth of Knowledge Winners\n</h3>\n\n\n<div>\n\n  <br>\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@dannwaneri shares a hard-won lesson: don't let a misconfigured OpenClaw agent burn through $5,600 in API credits in a month due to a flawed assumption in a spec file. The post breaks down what went wrong and introduces a spec-writing habit that prevents runaway token costs before they start.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>OpenClaw Burned $5,600 of API Credits in One Month. Here's the Spec Habit That Prevents It.</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Daniel Nwaneri\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 22\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          OpenClaw Burned $5,600 of API Credits in One Month. Here's the Spec Habit That Prevents It.\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#discuss\n            #openclawchallenge\n            #devchallenge\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              22&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              7&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            8 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@nirbhay_gautam_2a9e232b95 makes the case for why they are done trusting cloud-based AI tools with personal data, and how OpenClaw became the alternative. It's a sharp, personal essay about data ownership, the tradeoffs of convenience, and what it actually means to run AI on your own terms.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>I'm a Final-Year CS Student — And I'm Done Letting AI Tools Own My Data</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Nirbhay Gautam\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 17\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          I'm a Final-Year CS Student — And I'm Done Letting AI Tools Own My Data\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #openclawchallenge\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              10&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              2&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            5 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n<div>\n\n  \n<p>@gramli walks through how to run OpenClaw locally using Windows Sandbox for secure, disposable isolation. The guide is practical and reproducible, making it a great reference for anyone cautious about running AI agents on their main machine.\n\n\n</p><div>\n  <p>Run OpenClaw Locally on Windows Using Windows Sandbox for Secure Isolation</p><div>\n      <p>OpenClaw Challenge Submission 🦞\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Daniel Balcarek\n            </p>\n\n          </div>\n          <p>Apr 27\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          Run OpenClaw Locally on Windows Using Windows Sandbox for Secure Isolation\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #openclawchallenge\n            #ai\n            #tutorial\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              31&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              11&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            8 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n<br>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Prizes\n</h2>\n\n<p>Each winner will receive:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>$200 USD</li>\n<li>DEV++ Membership</li>\n<li>Exclusive DEV Winner Badge</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>All participants with a valid submission will receive a completion badge on their DEV profile.</p>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  What's Next?\n</h2>\n\n<p>The Gemma 4 Challenge is live! Whether you love to build or love to write, there's a prompt for you and a $3,000 prize pool up for grabs!</p>\n\n\n<div>\n  <p>Join the Gemma 4 Challenge: $3,000 prize pool for TEN winners!</p><div>\n      <p>Announcing the Gemma 4 Challenge\n\n</p><div>\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Jess Lee\n            </p>\n\n            <p><span>\n              <span> for </span>The DEV Team\n            </span>\n          </p></div>\n          <p>May 6\n        </p></div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h2>\n        \n          Join the Gemma 4 Challenge: $3,000 prize pool for TEN winners!\n        \n      </h2>\n        <p>#devchallenge\n            #gemmachallenge\n            #gemma\n        </p>\n      <div>\n        <p>\n            \n              \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n                  \n                    \n                  \n              \n              452&nbsp;reactions\n            \n          \n            \n              \n\n              105&nbsp;comments\n            \n        </p>\n        <p><small>\n            5 min read\n          </small>\n            \n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<p>Thank you for participating! See you next time. 🦞</p>\n\n\n            </div>\n\n              \n          </div>\n          \n\n\n\n\n        </article>\n\n        \n\n          <!-- Bottom content skipped via SKIP_BOTTOM_CONTENT config -->\n      </div>\n    </main>\n\n    \n  </div></div>",
