    "date": "2026-05-01T00:02:24.000Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "tech_devto_3500926",
    "source": "Dev.to (machinelearning)",
    "category": "Technology",
    "title": "How I Built an Autonomous Dataset Generator with CrewAI + Ollama (72-hour run, 1,065 entries)",
    "url": "https://dev.to/robopilingui/how-i-built-an-autonomous-dataset-generator-with-crewai-ollama-72-hour-run-1065-entries-2280",
    "text": "<div><div>\n                <h2>\n  \n  \n  Background\n</h2>\n\n<p>I needed high-quality instruction datasets for fine-tuning local LLMs, but commercial options were prohibitively expensive ($500-2,000 for decent quality datasets). </p>\n\n<p>So I asked myself: <em>What if I could build a system that generates these datasets autonomously while I sleep?</em></p>\n\n<p><strong>Result:</strong> 1,065 professional instruction/response pairs in 72 hours, 100% local, zero API costs.</p>\n\n<p>Here's exactly how I did it.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  The Problem with Existing Datasets\n</h2>\n\n<p>When you want to fine-tune a local LLM for specific tasks, you face three options:</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Use generic datasets</strong> → Don't match your domain</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Manual creation</strong> → Exhausting, slow, doesn't scale</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Buy commercial datasets</strong> → Expensive ($500-2,000), limited customization</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>I wanted code instruction pairs with:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Python/AI/ML/DevOps/Database topics</li>\n<li>Chain-of-Thought reasoning (not just answers)</li>\n<li>Real-world complexity (no template responses)</li>\n<li>Continuous generation (24/7 if possible)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>None of the existing options delivered all four.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  The Solution: Multi-Agent Autonomous System\n</h2>\n\n<p>I built a three-agent system inspired by academic research workflows:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code>┌──────────────────┐\n│   Curator        │ ← Selects topics from knowledge base\n│   (Qwen 7B)      │\n└────────┬─────────┘\n         │\n         ▼\n┌──────────────────┐\n│   Producer       │ ← Generates instruction + response + CoT\n│   (Qwen 7B)      │\n└────────┬─────────┘\n         │\n         ▼\n┌──────────────────┐\n│   Critic         │ ← Validates logic, checks hallucinations\n│   (DeepSeek 1.5B)│\n└────────┬─────────┘\n         │\n         ▼\n    [Accept/Reject]\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Agent Roles\n</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Curator Agent:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Reads ChromaDB vector store of potential topics</li>\n<li>Selects next topic based on diversity + priority</li>\n<li>Prevents duplicates via similarity search</li>\n<li>Think of it as a research librarian</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Producer Agent:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Generates the actual instruction/response pair</li>\n<li>Includes Chain-of-Thought reasoning</li>\n<li>Uses domain knowledge to create realistic scenarios</li>\n<li>Think of it as the expert writer</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Critic Agent:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Reviews Producer's output for:\n\n<ul>\n<li>Hallucinations</li>\n<li>Logical errors</li>\n<li>Incomplete reasoning</li>\n<li>Generic template responses</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n</li>\n\n<li>Binary decision: Accept or Reject</li>\n\n<li>Think of it as the peer reviewer</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Tech Stack\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Core Components\n</h3>\n\n\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span># 1. Ollama (Local LLM Engine)\n# Custom Modelfiles with 8k context:\n</span><span>qwen2</span><span>.</span><span>5</span><span>-</span><span>coder</span><span>-</span><span>8</span><span>k</span><span>:</span><span>7</span><span>b</span>    <span># 4.7GB, main generator\n</span><span>deepseek</span><span>-</span><span>r1</span><span>-</span><span>8</span><span>k</span><span>:</span><span>1.5</span><span>b</span>     <span># 1.1GB, validator\n</span>\n<span># 2. CrewAI (Agent Orchestration)\n</span><span>from</span> <span>crewai</span> <span>import</span> <span>Agent</span><span>,</span> <span>Crew</span><span>,</span> <span>Task</span>\n\n<span># 3. ChromaDB (Deduplication + Memory)\n</span><span>from</span> <span>chromadb</span> <span>import</span> <span>Client</span>\n\n<span># 4. Flask (Real-time Dashboard)\n</span><span>from</span> <span>flask</span> <span>import</span> <span>Flask</span><span>,</span> <span>render_template</span>\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Hardware\n</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>AMD Ryzen AI 9 HX 370</strong> (12 cores, 32GB RAM shared as VRAM)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Mini PC</strong> (Geekom A9 Max, ~$899)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>SSD NVMe</strong> (for fast model loading)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Total investment: <strong>$899 + ~$3.60 electricity for 72 hours</strong></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Implementation Details\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Challenge 1: Memory Leaks in Long Runs\n</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Agent instances accumulate state. After ~100 cycles, performance degrades → crashes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Solution:</strong> Recreate all agents every cycle.<br>\n</p>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span>from</span> <span>crewai</span> <span>import</span> <span>Agent</span><span>,</span> <span>Crew</span><span>,</span> <span>Task</span>\n\n<span>for</span> <span>cycle</span> <span>in</span> <span>range</span><span>(</span><span>1000</span><span>):</span>\n    <span># Recreate agents from scratch (prevents memory leaks)\n</span>    <span>curator</span> <span>=</span> <span>Agent</span><span>(</span>\n        <span>role</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Topic Curator</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span>\n        <span>goal</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Select next topic to generate</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span>\n        <span>llm</span><span>=</span><span>ollama_qwen</span>\n    <span>)</span>\n\n    <span>producer</span> <span>=</span> <span>Agent</span><span>(</span>\n        <span>role</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Content Producer</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span> \n        <span>goal</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Generate high-quality instruction pair</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span>\n        <span>llm</span><span>=</span><span>ollama_qwen</span>\n    <span>)</span>\n\n    <span>critic</span> <span>=</span> <span>Agent</span><span>(</span>\n        <span>role</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Quality Critic</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span>\n        <span>goal</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Validate logic and catch hallucinations</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span>\n        <span>llm</span><span>=</span><span>ollama_deepseek</span>\n    <span>)</span>\n\n    <span># Define sequential workflow\n</span>    <span>tasks</span> <span>=</span> <span>[</span>\n        <span>Task</span><span>(</span><span>description</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Select topic</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span> <span>agent</span><span>=</span><span>curator</span><span>),</span>\n        <span>Task</span><span>(</span><span>description</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Generate content</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span> <span>agent</span><span>=</span><span>producer</span><span>),</span>\n        <span>Task</span><span>(</span><span>description</span><span>=</span><span>\"</span><span>Validate quality</span><span>\"</span><span>,</span> <span>agent</span><span>=</span><span>critic</span><span>)</span>\n    <span>]</span>\n\n    <span>crew</span> <span>=</span> <span>Crew</span><span>(</span><span>agents</span><span>=</span><span>[</span><span>curator</span><span>,</span> <span>producer</span><span>,</span> <span>critic</span><span>],</span> <span>tasks</span><span>=</span><span>tasks</span><span>)</span>\n    <span>result</span> <span>=</span> <span>crew</span><span>.</span><span>kickoff</span><span>()</span>\n\n    <span># Explicit cleanup\n</span>    <span>del</span> <span>crew</span><span>,</span> <span>curator</span><span>,</span> <span>producer</span><span>,</span> <span>critic</span>\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Result:</strong> Zero crashes in 72 hours. Stable RAM at 24.2 GB.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Challenge 2: CrewAI + Ollama Compatibility\n</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Problem:</strong> CrewAI v1.12+ requires string-only responses, but Ollama returns objects by default.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Solution:</strong> Embed configuration in Modelfiles (permanent fix).<br>\n</p>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span># Modelfile for qwen2.5-coder-8k:7b</span>\n<span>FROM</span><span> qwen2.5-coder:7b</span>\n\nPARAMETER num_ctx 8192\nPARAMETER temperature 0.7\nPARAMETER top_p 0.9\n\nSYSTEM \"\"\"You are an expert programmer...\"\"\"\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Run:<br>\n</p>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code>ollama create qwen2.5-coder-8k:7b <span>-f</span> Modelfile_qwen\nollama create deepseek-r1-8k:1.5b <span>-f</span> Modelfile_deepseek\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>This makes <code>num_ctx: 8192</code> permanent at the model level. No runtime config needed.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Challenge 3: Duplicate Questions\n</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Problem:</strong> Random topic generation creates duplicates.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Solution:</strong> ChromaDB similarity search + rejection.<br>\n</p>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span>import</span> <span>chromadb</span>\n\n<span>client</span> <span>=</span> <span>chromadb</span><span>.</span><span>Client</span><span>()</span>\n<span>collection</span> <span>=</span> <span>client</span><span>.</span><span>create_collection</span><span>(</span><span>\"</span><span>generated_questions</span><span>\"</span><span>)</span>\n\n<span>def</span> <span>is_duplicate</span><span>(</span><span>new_question</span><span>,</span> <span>threshold</span><span>=</span><span>0.85</span><span>):</span>\n    <span>\"\"\"</span><span>Check if question already exists via embedding similarity</span><span>\"\"\"</span>\n    <span>results</span> <span>=</span> <span>collection</span><span>.</span><span>query</span><span>(</span>\n        <span>query_texts</span><span>=</span><span>[</span><span>new_question</span><span>],</span>\n        <span>n_results</span><span>=</span><span>1</span>\n    <span>)</span>\n\n    <span>if</span> <span>not</span> <span>results</span><span>[</span><span>'</span><span>ids</span><span>'</span><span>]:</span>\n        <span>return</span> <span>False</span>\n\n    <span>similarity</span> <span>=</span> <span>results</span><span>[</span><span>'</span><span>distances</span><span>'</span><span>][</span><span>0</span><span>][</span><span>0</span><span>]</span>\n    <span>return</span> <span>similarity</span> <span>&gt;</span> <span>threshold</span>\n\n<span># Before saving\n</span><span>if</span> <span>not</span> <span>is_duplicate</span><span>(</span><span>instruction</span><span>):</span>\n    <span>save_to_dataset</span><span>(</span><span>entry</span><span>)</span>\n    <span>collection</span><span>.</span><span>add</span><span>(</span>\n        <span>documents</span><span>=</span><span>[</span><span>instruction</span><span>],</span>\n        <span>ids</span><span>=</span><span>[</span><span>unique_id</span><span>]</span>\n    <span>)</span>\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Result:</strong> 452 unique topics across 1,065 entries (zero duplicates).</p>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  🔥 Update (April 20, 2026)\n</h2>\n\n<p><strong>The system kept running.</strong></p>\n\n<p>After the initial 72-hour run, I left the autonomous system active. Six days later, it had generated <strong>2,772 total entries</strong> — a <strong>160% increase</strong> from the original dataset.</p>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  New Metrics\n</h3>\n\n<div><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Original (72h)</th>\n<th><strong>Now (9 days)</strong></th>\n<th>Growth</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total Entries</strong></td>\n<td>1,065</td>\n<td><strong>2,772</strong></td>\n<td>\n<strong>+160%</strong> 🚀</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Python</strong></td>\n<td>346</td>\n<td><strong>925</strong></td>\n<td>+167%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AI/ML</strong></td>\n<td>287</td>\n<td><strong>725</strong></td>\n<td>+153%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Database</strong></td>\n<td>99</td>\n<td><strong>310</strong></td>\n<td>+213%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Backend/API</strong></td>\n<td>126</td>\n<td><strong>296</strong></td>\n<td>+135%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DevOps/Cloud</strong></td>\n<td>99</td>\n<td><strong>225</strong></td>\n<td>+127%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Other</strong></td>\n<td>108</td>\n<td><strong>291</strong></td>\n<td>+169%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>System Stability</strong></td>\n<td>0 crashes</td>\n<td><strong>0 crashes</strong></td>\n<td>✅</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n\n<p><strong>Key insight:</strong> The autonomous architecture proved its long-term viability. Zero crashes, consistent quality (acceptance rate remained ~50%), and continuous 24/7 generation while I worked on other projects.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Updated free datasets:</strong> All 5 HuggingFace LITE repos now contain the expanded data (462, 362, 155, 148, 112 entries respectively). Check the links below for the latest versions.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Results After 72 Hours\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Metrics\n</h3>\n\n<div><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total Entries</strong></td>\n<td>1,065</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Success Rate</strong></td>\n<td>50.9% (605 accepted / 460 rejected)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Unique Topics</strong></td>\n<td>452</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Velocity</strong></td>\n<td>14.4 entries/hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RAM Usage</strong></td>\n<td>24.2 GB (stable)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CPU Usage</strong></td>\n<td>31.1% average</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Crashes</strong></td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Distribution by Category\n</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Python:</strong> 346 entries (33%)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>AI/ML:</strong> 287 entries (27%)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Backend/API:</strong> 126 entries (12%)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Database/SQL:</strong> 99 entries (9%)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>DevOps/Cloud:</strong> 99 entries (9%)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Other:</strong> 108 entries (10%)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Quality Samples\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Example 1: Python Development\n</h3>\n\n\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span>{</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"instruction\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"How to create a Dockerfile for a Python application?\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"input\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"output\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"# Step-by-step guide to create a production-ready Dockerfile:</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>1. **Choose Base Image**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   - Use official Python image: `python:3.11-slim`</span><span>\\n</span><span>   - For smaller size: `python:3.11-alpine`</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>2. **Set Working Directory**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   WORKDIR /app</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>3. **Copy Requirements First** (leverage Docker cache)</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   COPY requirements.txt .</span><span>\\n</span><span>   RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>4. **Copy Application Code**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   COPY . .</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>5. **Set Environment Variables**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ENV PORT=8000</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>6. **Expose Port**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   EXPOSE $PORT</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>7. **Define Entrypoint**</span><span>\\n</span><span>   ```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>   CMD [</span><span>\\\"</span><span>python</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>app.py</span><span>\\\"</span><span>]</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n   ```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**Complete Example:**</span><span>\\n</span><span>```\n\ndockerfile</span><span>\\n</span><span>FROM python:3.11-slim</span><span>\\n</span><span>WORKDIR /app</span><span>\\n</span><span>COPY requirements.txt .</span><span>\\n</span><span>RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt</span><span>\\n</span><span>COPY . .</span><span>\\n</span><span>ENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1</span><span>\\n</span><span>EXPOSE 8000</span><span>\\n</span><span>CMD [</span><span>\\\"</span><span>uvicorn</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>main:app</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>--host</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>0.0.0.0</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>--port</span><span>\\\"</span><span>, </span><span>\\\"</span><span>8000</span><span>\\\"</span><span>]</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n```</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**Best Practices:**</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Use multi-stage builds for smaller images</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Don't run as root (create user)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Use .dockerignore to exclude unnecessary files</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Pin dependency versions in requirements.txt\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n\n  </span><span>\"thought\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"User needs containerization setup. Key considerations: 1) Layer caching optimization (copy requirements first), 2) Security (non-root user), 3) Image size (slim vs alpine tradeoff), 4) Production readiness (health checks, signals). Template should be practical and immediately usable.\"</span><span>\n</span><span>}</span><span>\n</span></code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Character counts:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Output: 928 chars</li>\n<li>Thought: 266 chars</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Example 2: AI/ML Engineering\n</h3>\n\n\n\n<div>\n<pre><code><span>{</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"instruction\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"Explain the difference between EC2 instances and Lambda functions for ML model deployment\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"input\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n  </span><span>\"output\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"**EC2 Instances vs Lambda for ML Deployment:**</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**EC2 Instances (Virtual Machines)**</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Pros:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Full control over environment (custom libraries, CUDA, etc.)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- No execution time limits</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Better for large models (multi-GB)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- GPU support (P3, G4 instances)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Persistent connections (WebSockets, streaming)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Predictable latency</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Cons:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Always running = always paying ($50-500+/month)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Manual scaling configuration</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Need to manage OS, security patches</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Cold start when scaling from 0</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Best for:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Real-time inference with steady traffic</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Models &gt;1GB</span><span>\\n</span><span>- GPU-intensive workloads</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Long-running predictions (&gt;15 min)</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**Lambda Functions (Serverless)**</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Pros:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Pay per invocation ($0.20 per 1M requests)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Auto-scaling (0 to thousands)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- No server management</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Built-in HA/fault tolerance</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Cons:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- 15-minute timeout</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Limited to 10GB RAM</span><span>\\n</span><span>- No GPU support</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Cold starts (1-5 seconds)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Package size limit (250MB unzipped)</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>*Best for:*</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Batch predictions</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Small models (&lt;100MB)</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Sporadic/unpredictable traffic</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Budget constraints</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**Hybrid Approach:**</span><span>\\n</span><span>Use SageMaker Serverless Inference:</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Lambda-like pricing</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Support for larger models</span><span>\\n</span><span>- Automatic scaling</span><span>\\n</span><span>- GPU available</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>**Decision Tree:**</span><span>\\n</span><span>```\n\n</span><span>\\n</span><span>Model size &gt;1GB? → EC2</span><span>\\n</span><span>GPU required? → EC2</span><span>\\n</span><span>Constant traffic? → EC2</span><span>\\n</span><span>Budget &lt;$50/mo? → Lambda</span><span>\\n</span><span>Unpredictable spikes? → Lambda</span><span>\\n</span><span>\n\n```\"</span><span>,</span><span>\n\n  </span><span>\"thought\"</span><span>:</span><span> </span><span>\"User comparing infrastructure options for ML deployment. Critical factors: cost structure (fixed vs pay-per-use), model size constraints, GPU requirements, latency tolerance, traffic patterns. Should provide concrete decision criteria and mention SageMaker Serverless as middle ground. Real-world cost examples help contextualize.\"</span><span>\n</span><span>}</span><span>\n</span></code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Character counts:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Output: 1,876 chars</li>\n<li>Thought: 261 chars</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Cost Comparison\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  My Approach (Local)\n</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Hardware:</strong> $899 one-time (reusable forever)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Electricity:</strong> $3.60 for 72 hours</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Per entry:</strong> $0.85 amortized (or $0.003 electricity only)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Commercial APIs (for 1,065 entries)\n</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>GPT-4 API:</strong> ~$850 (800 tokens avg × $0.001/token × 1,065)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Claude API:</strong> ~$1,200 (longer responses × higher price)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>OpenRouter DeepSeek:</strong> ~$150 (cheapest API option)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Savings: 99%+ (after hardware pays for itself in 2-3 runs)</strong></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Lessons Learned\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  1. Quality Over Quantity\n</h3>\n\n<p>A 50.9% rejection rate seems harsh, but it's a <strong>feature, not a bug</strong>.</p>\n\n<p>The Critic agent catches:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>❌ Hallucinated facts (\"Python 4.0 was released...\")</li>\n<li>❌ Incomplete reasoning ('Just use library X\" without explanation)</li>\n<li>❌ Generic templates (\"Here are 5 steps...\")</li>\n<li>❌ Logic errors (contradictory statements)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Only entries that pass rigorous validation make it through.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Result:</strong> Every entry is production-quality.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  2. Hardware Performs Better Than Expected\n</h3>\n\n<p>I was skeptical about running two LLMs simultaneously on 32GB RAM. Turns out AMD's shared VRAM architecture works great:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>During generation:</strong> 24.2 GB RAM (87% utilization)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>CPU:</strong> 31.1% average (not maxed, room for optimization)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Cycle time:</strong> ~6 minutes per entry (2 models sequentially)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Stability:</strong> Zero crashes in 72 hours</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For comparison, this would cost $40-100/month in cloud GPU time.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  3. Automation Compounds\n</h3>\n\n<p>The system ran while I:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Slept (8 hours × 3 nights = ~400 entries)</li>\n<li>Worked (8 hours × 3 days = ~400 entries)</li>\n<li>Coded other projects (8 hours × 3 days = ~265 entries)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Total: 1,065 entries with ~10 minutes of manual intervention (checking dashboard once/day).</p>\n\n<p><strong>That's the power of autonomous systems.</strong></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Free Datasets Released\n</h2>\n\n<p>I just uploaded <strong>5 LITE versions (50% of data, 100% free)</strong> to HuggingFace:</p>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  🐍 Python Developer Dataset\n</h3>\n\n<p>173 entries covering:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Docker/containerization</li>\n<li>Testing patterns</li>\n<li>API development</li>\n<li>Package management</li>\n<li>Best practices</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  🤖 AI/ML Engineering Dataset\n</h3>\n\n<p>143 entries covering:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Model deployment (EC2, Lambda, SageMaker)</li>\n<li>MLOps patterns</li>\n<li>Training optimization</li>\n<li>Cloud ML services</li>\n<li>LLM fine-tuning</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  ☁️ DevOps &amp; Cloud Dataset\n</h3>\n\n<p>49 entries covering:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>CI/CD pipelines</li>\n<li>Infrastructure as Code</li>\n<li>Kubernetes/Docker</li>\n<li>Monitoring &amp; logging</li>\n<li>AWS/GCP/Azure</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  🔌 Backend &amp; API Dataset\n</h3>\n\n<p>63 entries covering:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>REST/GraphQL design</li>\n<li>Authentication patterns</li>\n<li>Database optimization</li>\n<li>Caching strategies</li>\n<li>Microservices</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  💾 Database &amp; SQL Dataset\n</h3>\n\n<p>49 entries covering:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Query optimization</li>\n<li>Schema design</li>\n<li>Transactions &amp; ACID</li>\n<li>NoSQL patterns</li>\n<li>Performance tuning</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><p><strong>Format:</strong> JSONL with <code>instruction</code>, <code>input</code>, <code>output</code>, <code>thought</code> fields</p><p>\n<strong>License:</strong> MIT (use however you want)</p><p>\n<strong>Ready for:</strong> HuggingFace Transformers, Axolotl, LLaMA Factory</p></div>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  What's Next?\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  V2 Features (in progress)\n</h3>\n\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Multilingual datasets</strong> (Spanish, French, German)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Difficulty levels</strong> (Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Custom domains</strong> (on-demand generation for specific niches)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Video tutorials</strong> (system walkthrough + setup guide)</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Open-Source Plans\n</h3>\n\n<p>If there's enough interest, I'll release:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Complete agent definitions</li>\n<li>Modelfile configurations</li>\n<li>ChromaDB setup scripts</li>\n<li>Dashboard code (Flask + real-time metrics)</li>\n<li>Consolidation scripts (JSONL → categorized products)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Update:</strong> Based on comments, I'll publish setup guide by end of week.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Try It Yourself\n</h2>\n\n<h3>\n  \n  \n  Quick Start\n</h3>\n\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Download a dataset:</strong>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code>   wget https://huggingface.co/datasets/bernabepuente/python-instruction-dataset/resolve/main/dataset.jsonl\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Load in Python:</strong>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code>   <span>import</span> <span>json</span>\n\n   <span>with</span> <span>open</span><span>(</span><span>'</span><span>dataset.jsonl</span><span>'</span><span>,</span> <span>'</span><span>r</span><span>'</span><span>)</span> <span>as</span> <span>f</span><span>:</span>\n       <span>data</span> <span>=</span> <span>[</span><span>json</span><span>.</span><span>loads</span><span>(</span><span>line</span><span>)</span> <span>for</span> <span>line</span> <span>in</span> <span>f</span><span>]</span>\n\n   <span>print</span><span>(</span><span>f</span><span>\"</span><span>Loaded </span><span>{</span><span>len</span><span>(</span><span>data</span><span>)</span><span>}</span><span> entries</span><span>\"</span><span>)</span>\n   <span>print</span><span>(</span><span>f</span><span>\"</span><span>Sample: </span><span>{</span><span>data</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span><span>}</span><span>\"</span><span>)</span>\n</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Fine-tune with Transformers:</strong>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div>\n<pre><code>   <span>from</span> <span>transformers</span> <span>import</span> <span>AutoTokenizer</span><span>,</span> <span>AutoModelForCausalLM</span><span>,</span> <span>Trainer</span>\n\n   <span># Load your base model\n</span>   <span>model</span> <span>=</span> <span>AutoModelForCausalLM</span><span>.</span><span>from_pretrained</span><span>(</span><span>\"</span><span>meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf</span><span>\"</span><span>)</span>\n   <span>tokenizer</span> <span>=</span> <span>AutoTokenizer</span><span>.</span><span>from_pretrained</span><span>(</span><span>\"</span><span>meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf</span><span>\"</span><span>)</span>\n\n   <span># Prepare dataset\n</span>   <span>def</span> <span>format_prompt</span><span>(</span><span>entry</span><span>):</span>\n       <span>return</span> <span>f</span><span>\"</span><span>Instruction: </span><span>{</span><span>entry</span><span>[</span><span>'</span><span>instruction</span><span>'</span><span>]</span><span>}</span><span>\\n\\n</span><span>Response: </span><span>{</span><span>entry</span><span>[</span><span>'</span><span>output</span><span>'</span><span>]</span><span>}</span><span>\"</span>\n\n   <span># Train!\n</span>   <span># (full training code in dataset README)\n</span></code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Questions I'm Happy to Answer\n</h2>\n\n<p>Drop a comment if you want to know about:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Optimizing Ollama for long runs</li>\n<li>CrewAI agent patterns for production</li>\n<li>ChromaDB deduplication strategies</li>\n<li>Dataset quality validation</li>\n<li>Hardware recommendations for local LLM workflows</li>\n<li>Monetization experiments (Scale AI, Gumroad, HF Premium)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<h2>\n  \n  \n  Conclusion\n</h2>\n\n<p>Building autonomous systems that work while you sleep is incredibly satisfying.</p>\n\n<p>This project taught me:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Local LLMs can match commercial quality (with good prompts)</li>\n<li>Multi-agent validation catches errors humans would miss</li>\n<li>Hardware investment pays for itself quickly</li>\n<li>Automation compounds exponentially</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><p><strong>Total time invested:</strong> ~20 hours (setup + monitoring)</p><p>\n<strong>Total output:</strong> 1,065 professional datasets</p><p>\n<strong>Time per entry:</strong> 1.1 minutes of human time</p></div>\n\n<p>Try the datasets and let me know what you think!</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n<p><strong>Links:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>🎁 Free Datasets: https://huggingface.co/bernabepuente\n</li>\n<li>📧 Contact: (tu email o Twitter)</li>\n<li>💬 Discuss: Comments below!</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Tech Stack:</strong><br>\nOllama • CrewAI • ChromaDB • Flask • Python 3.11 • AMD Ryzen AI 9</p>\n\n<p><strong>License:</strong> MIT (all datasets)</p>\n\n\n            </div></div>",
