    "title": "Edit, compile & play Quake III maps in your browser.",
    "url": "https://q3edit.com",
    "text": "<div><div>\n    \n\n    <section>\n      <div>\n        \n        <p>\n          Open, edit, and save real <code>.map</code> files — brushes, patches,\n          entities, and terrain in a TypeScript + WebGL2 editor, with BSP\n          compilation by id Software's original q3map compiled to WebAssembly.\n          One click launches your compiled map in browser-native ioquake3.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n            Launch Q3Edit \n          \n          <span>No game files needed — ships with OpenArena assets. Requires WebGL2.</span>\n        </p>\n        <ul>\n          <li><span>01</span> Radiant-style four-view UI</li>\n          <li><span>02</span> Brushes, patches, CSG, terrain</li>\n          <li><span>03</span> q3map + ioquake3 in WASM</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <p><img>\n        </p>\n        <p><span></span> The editor running in a browser tab</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section>\n      <div>\n        <h2>Build maps with Codex or Claude.</h2>\n        <p>\n          Connect an AI coding agent to the map open in Q3Edit. The agent can\n          inspect, create, texture, validate, compile, and playtest geometry\n          while every atomic edit appears live in the browser and remains\n          available through normal undo.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          MCP setup instructions \n        \n      </p></div>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>01</span><div><p><strong>Run the local companion</strong></p><p>Your maps, compiler, assets, and activity logs stay on your computer.</p></div></li>\n        <li><span>02</span><div><p><strong>Connect Q3Edit</strong></p><p>Enter the pairing code in View → Local MCP Connection, or use the printed editor URL.</p></div></li>\n        <li><span>03</span><div><p><strong>Describe the map</strong></p><p>Use Codex, Claude Code, or any compatible MCP client to author and review it.</p></div></li>\n      </ol>\n    </section>\n\n    \n  </div></div>",
